=== 1. Theorem A, Fourier rank check: n (x) a + a (x) n traceless-sym = 0  => a = 0 for n != 0 ===
d=2: minimal rank over n in [-3,3]^d minus 0 = 2 (= d means trivial kernel)
d=3: minimal rank over n in [-3,3]^d minus 0 = 3 (= d means trivial kernel)
gradient case p = grad u: mode n contributes u_n (n n^T)_traceless, zero iff n = 0 (d>=2).
Lattice form: E_g protected pointwise <=> only |n_x|=|n_y|=|n_z| modes (body-diagonal hopping);
              T_2g protected pointwise <=> only modes with one nonzero component (axis hopping);
              both <=> u constant.

=== 2. the two pointwise-protected classes and their unprotected channel (m = 1) ===
axis-only (separable nn): muE, muT2 = (np.float64(0.001970388641878533), np.float64(-0.0))
body-diagonal-only (u = 1 - cos x cos y cos z): muE, muT2 = (np.float64(3.193346304787127e-21), np.float64(0.0006011748785883808))
exact body-diagonal symbol: muE, muT2, min u = (np.float64(-0.0), np.float64(0.0006011748823967418), np.float64(0.0036092803549254704))
  note: zeros of u at (0,0,0),(pi,pi,0),(pi,0,pi),(0,pi,pi): 4 decoupled sublattices (doubling)

