=== 6. density-weight family: transport eps as weight-w density, mu^(w) = (1-w) mu_0 - w(1-w) <eps (div v)^2> ===
  w=0.0: muE = +1.970389e-03   (muT2 = 0 for separable, all w)
  w=0.25: muE = -6.003172e-02   (muT2 = 0 for separable, all w)
  w=0.5: muE = -8.102749e-02   (muT2 = 0 for separable, all w)
  w=0.75: muE = -6.101692e-02   (muT2 = 0 for separable, all w)
  w=1.0: muE = +0.000000e+00   (muT2 = 0 for separable, all w)
  root of mu^(w)=0 in (0,1): 0.005970492516326183  (a tuned weight, mass dependent)
  linear term of weight-w transport: T1 = -(L_v eps) - w eps div v; extra per-quantum symbol -w omega (h:Hess u)/2 is not
  a conserved-stress term (nonzero uniform total) -> breaks RN-L1 exact stress unless w = 0 on the operator.
